@startuml Doctor Patient Access Granting
actor Doctor
participant Browser

participant RAG


participant nginx
' participant oauth2Proxy

' participant Keycloak

participant NodeJS as NJS

participant PatientDataRedis as PDR

participant FHIR

participant AccessRedis as AR

participant RAGRedis as RR

participant AuditLog

participant Application as App
actor Patient

==Access Granting Flow (FHIR R4 Consent Standard)==
Patient -> App : Grant access to Dr (search by doctor ID)
App -> nginx : access grant creation req\n{doctorId, scopes[], resourceTypes[], purpose[], expiresIn}
nginx -> NJS : forward request with patient's access token

NJS -> NJS : validate patient token & extract patientId
NJS -> FHIR : Verify patient owns their data (GET /Patient/{patientId})
FHIR -> NJS : Patient resource confirmed

NJS -> NJS : Validate requested scopes/purposes against patient's rights

NJS -> App : Request patient verification\n(e.g., 2FA, PIN, biometric, or review Consent Form)
App -> Patient : Display Consent Form\n"Grant Dr. X access to [Conditions, Encounters]\nfor Treatment purposes until [date]"
Patient -> App : Confirm (sign/verify)
App -> NJS : Verification confirmed

NJS -> FHIR : Create Consent resource (FHIR R4)\n{\n  status: "active",\n  grantor: Patient,\n  grantee: Practitioner/doctorId,\n  decision: "permit",\n  provision: {\n    actor: doctorId,\n    purpose: ["TREAT"],\n    resourceType: ["Condition","Encounter"],\n    period: {start, end}\n  },\n  verification: {\n    verified: true,\n    verificationType: "Patient signature",\n    verificationDate: now\n  }\n}
FHIR -> NJS : Consent resource created with consentId

' access:grant:{patientId}:{doctorId}\nValue: {grantId, scopes, expiresAt}\nTTL: patient-specified duration
' grantId : specific value for currently active session
NJS -> NJS : Generate grant signature (HMAC of consentId+scope+expiry)
NJS -> AR : Cache access grant for fast lookup\nKey: access:grant:{patientId}:{doctorId}\nValue: {consentId, scopes, expiresAt, signature}\nTTL: patient-specified duration
AR -> NJS : Grant cached successfully

' event\n{patientId, doctorId, consentId, timestamp, scopes, purposes, verification} , hal me7tagen keda tho?
NJS -> AuditLog : Log consent grant 
AuditLog -> NJS : Logged successfully

NJS -> nginx : Creation Confirmation {consentId}
nginx -> App : Grant created successfully
App -> Patient : Display confirmation\n"Dr. X can now access your [Conditions, Encounters]\nConsent ID: {consentId}"

==Registered Doctor requesting access to patient data==
Doctor -> Browser : search for patient (by id)
Browser -> nginx : req to access patient data 
nginx-> NJS: forward req

NJS -> NJS : Extract doctorId from token
NJS -> FHIR : Query Consent resources\nWHERE performer=doctorId AND status=active
FHIR -> NJS : Return matching Consent resources (consentId, patient ref)

alt Doctor has access to patient data
NJS -> AR : Get cached grant for validation\nKey: access:grant:{patientId}:{doctorId}
AR -> NJS: return access grant with signature

NJS -> NJS : Verify signature (HMAC), validate scopes, check expiry

NJS -> FHIR : Fetch scoped resources only\n(e.g., Condition, Encounter per Consent.provision)
FHIR -> NJS : Return scoped patient data

NJS -> PDR : Cache scoped data only
NJS -> NJS : Preprocess scoped data for RAG
NJS -> RR : Store preprocessed scoped data

NJS -> AuditLog : Log data 
' access\n{doctorId, patientId, timestamp, resourceTypes, consentId}

NJS -> nginx: forward OK response with scoped data
nginx -> Browser: forward resp
Browser -> Doctor: display requested patient data 


' redis auto deletes expired data , double check :/

' else Access Grant expired 
' AR->NJS: 


else Doctor has no access to this pateint's data
AR->NJS: return no active consent found

' NJS -> AuditLog : Log unauthorized access attempt\n{doctorId, searchedPatientId, timestamp}
NJS -> nginx: return OK resp (mask patient's existence)
nginx -> Browser: forward resp (empty)
Browser -> Doctor : display empty results (e.g no patient found)

end

