==Doctor chooses report node==

==LLM queries (after dr opens patient graph , start llm session?)==
Doctor -> Browser : Ask question about patient
Browser -> RAG : Send query with question

RAG -> nginx : Request patient data (with access token)
nginx -> NJS : Forward request with doctorId from token

NJS -> FHIR : Verify active Consent\nWHERE performer=doctorId AND patient=patientId AND status=active
alt Valid active Consent
FHIR -> NJS : Consent still active
NJS -> RR : Get preprocessed scoped data
RR -> NJS : Return scoped patient data

NJS -> AuditLog : Log RAG access\n{doctorId, patientId, timestamp, queryType, consentId}

NJS -> nginx : Forward scoped data
nginx -> RAG : Forward scoped data
RAG -> RAG : Process query with scoped context
RAG -> Browser : Return LLM response
Browser -> Doctor : Display answer

else Consent revoked or expired
FHIR -> NJS : No active Consent
NJS -> nginx : Return unauthorized
nginx -> RAG : Forward unauthorized
RAG -> Browser : Display access denied
Browser -> Doctor : Show "Access revoked or expired"
end 

==Patient Revokes access==
' drs with access are listed??
Patient -> App : revoke dr access 

App -> nginx: request deletion of access grant
nginx -> NJS : forward deletion request

NJS -> FHIR : Update Consent resource to revoked\nPATCH /Consent/{consentId} {status: "inactive"}
FHIR -> NJS : Consent resource updated

NJS -> AR : Delete cached grant\nKey: access:grant:{patientId}:{doctorId}
AR -> NJS : deletion confirmation

NJS -> PDR : Invalidate cached patient data for this grant
NJS -> RR : Clear RAG preprocessed data for this grant

NJS -> AuditLog : Log access revocation\n{patientId, doctorId, timestamp, consentId, reason}

NJS-> nginx: return OK 
nginx-> App: forward OK response
App-> Patient: display revocation confirmation


